Missing: a request in a header is parsed through its includers

user.c includes header.h, and f is pushed on in header.h. Then user.c is rewritten on
disk without the include, and f is pushed on in header.h again. Pass 3 strips header.h,
since user.c is still known as its includer and is built again. Then singlePass() parses
header.h on its own, as the request file, and header.h:1 comes back.

ADR-0032 (amended 2026-10-11) says a file that is not a CU is never parsed on its own,
the request file included. It is parsed through the CUs that include it, with the cursor
in it, as a cursor in a macro body is today (collectCompilationUnitsExpandingTheMacro()
in src/server.c). With no includer, as here, the answer is a message saying that no
compilation unit includes the file.

expected is empty: write it when the message is worded. Backlog item
request-through-includers.
